      "content": "Those unexpected frequencies, often called inharmonic partials or \"ghost notes,\" introduce a slight metallic edge or shimmer that brain processes as unique instrument \"character\" or emotional nuance. Because they do not align perfectly with the harmonic spectrum, they create a subtle beating effect that gives the flute a living, iridescent quality rather than a pure, static tone. Listeners often associate this slight spectral complexity with the instrument's expressiveness and capability to convey subtle tensions or bluesy vibes within an accompaniment.",
